# Art guide: the noodle shop

Everything on the stream is drawn at 480x270 and shown at x4 with no smoothing.
One pixel is four screen pixels. The look is one image: a tall wooden noodle
shop at night, deep navy sky, near-black plum wood, red neon and paper
lanterns, one yellow kitchen window with the cook behind the counter, a blue
door, the vending machine's cyan, clutter at the sides. Dense, warm, dark.

## Palette

`assets/shop/palette.txt`, 36 keys in ramps that read dark to light. Pick three
tones from one ramp per material.

| Ramp | Keys | For |
|---|---|---|
| Night | `0` `1` `2` `3` `4` | outline and road (`0`), sky, horizon, mountains, pavement |
| Wood | `5` `6` `7` `8` `9` | walls (`5`-`7`), trim (`8`), warm posts, frames and the counter edge (`9`) |
| Roof | `a` `b` `c` | olive awning stripe, slate tiles and their highlights |
| Red | `d` `e` `f` `g` `h` `i` | deep shadow to neon core: lanterns, the disc, the banner, the mailbox |
| Yellow | `j` `k` `l` `m` | dim window, the kitchen light, the bright slats, white |
| Blue | `n` `o` `p` `q` | the door, its glow, the vending machine's cyan |
| Green | `r` `s` `t` | foliage dark to lit |
| Skin and misc | `u` `v` `w` `x` `y` `z` | skin, tan, metal, cream |

The keeper: hair `0`, skin `u`/`v`, white jacket `m` shaded `z`, blue apron
`o`/`n`, dark trousers `5`/`0`, boots `y`, red headband `f` with a `g` knot.
Nothing else in the shop wears white with a blue apron.

## Light

- The scene is lit from inside: the kitchen window (yellow), the neon (red), the
  door (blue), the vending machine (cyan). The sky is the only cool light.
  Sprites bake a hint of their own glow (a rim in the light's colour); the
  renderer adds pools on the pavement, halos in the air, streaks in the wet,
  from the list in `SceneView.lights()`.
- Shadow side is camera-right on everything.
- No baked ground shadows.

## Outline

- People and animals get a full one-pixel outline in `0` (the rig does it).
- Props: selective, `0` along the bottom row and the right side; the material's
  own darkest step on the top and left.
- The building has no outline; its depth comes from beams (`8`), posts (`9`)
  and the `5` shadow row under every eave.

## Sizes

| What | Size |
|---|---|
| The keeper | 16x36, feet on the bottom row, faces right |
| Passers-by | 16x36 (the kid 16x28), walk cycles of 6 at 6 to 8 fps |
| Customers | 14x30, seen from behind on a stool, 2 frames |
| Cat | 14x10: walk 4, sit 2, sleep 2 |
| Fixtures | bin 12x16 / 20x10 fallen, board 14x22, vending 18x32, mailbox 10x12, plants 14x16, door 26x37 |
| Bowl | 10x8, 4 frames of wisps |
| Building | two 480x240 scenery sprites, `shop_back` and `shop_front` |

Things that stand on the ground have a flat, fully painted bottom row. The
renderer puts that row on the row in `scene.ts` (`GROUND` for the pavement,
`PASSER_Y` a step closer to the camera, `BALCONY_Y` upstairs).

## Where things go

`src/shared/scene.ts` is the map. The kitchen opening is x 150..250, y
190..214; the counter runs 144..270 with stools at 156, 182, 208, 234; the door
is 284..310. The keeper stands behind the counter when `inside` (his legs are
hidden by it, the way a ramen counter works), on the pavement when `outside`,
on the balcony (y 112) when `upstairs`. Flags stand at six slots along the kerb.

## Animation

`fps:` in the sprite header; frames separated by `--`; `loop: no` holds the
last frame. Keeper modes and their sets in `assets/shop/keeper/`: idle (6),
walk (6), walk_bowl (6), talk (3), look (4, no loop), cook (4), serve (3),
wave (3), fix (4), kick (4, no loop), sweep (4), carry (6), read (3), sit (2),
nap (2), wipe (4). Missing sets fall back (`src/web/keeper.ts`).

Every frame must differ from its neighbour by at least two pixels moved or four
recoloured, or the change is lost at stream bitrates.

## The rigs

The art is code. `scripts/rig/shop.ts` paints the building with painters for
roofs, walls, lattice windows, lanterns and the bowl glyph; `people.ts` poses
figures from parts (arms, legs, head, held things) and outlines them;
`props.ts` draws the fixtures in each state, the bowl and the cat. `npm run
rig` runs them all and composes `dist/shop/preview.png`,
`keeper-sheet.png` and `props-sheet.png`; look at those before packing.

## Checking

- `npm run rig && npm run assets` with zero warnings for anything you touched.
- `dist/shop/preview.png`: does the building read at a glance, is the kitchen
  window the brightest thing, does the keeper read against the yellow.
- `npm run dev`, then `http://localhost:4400/?demo=1&hud=1` and the rain
  variant (`&weather=rain`): rain at night over the lit street is the worst
  case for both readability and frame time.
